Arm HVF on the macOS 12 floor (2ksbox, track M20 step 4, 2026-10-01).

QEMU 9.2's Arm Hypervisor.framework accelerator sizes the VM's IPA space
through the VM configuration calls macOS 13 added
(`hv_vm_config_create`, `hv_vm_config_{get_default,get_max,set}_ipa_size`)
and calls them unconditionally, so `aarch64-softmmu` does not compile
against our floor (`-Werror=unguarded-availability-new`, macOS 12 for
the community build) and would call a missing symbol on a macOS 12 host.
Each call now runs only under `__builtin_available(macOS 13, *)`; before
that the VM is made with no configuration, which is a 36-bit IPA space,
and a machine that needs more is refused with HV_UNSUPPORTED.
diff --git a/target/arm/hvf/hvf.c b/target/arm/hvf/hvf.c
index b00a7e1a84..5eaff55cba 100644
